{
  "requirement": "Usage MUST record mandatory input counts and sizes by evidence kind, in UTF-8\nbytes and lines, and the same information for additional inputs requested through\n`habeas` or `ripgrep`. A requirements input MUST also record its number of matched declarations.\nUsage MUST distinguish unique inputs from repeated reads, successful from\nfailed reads, and prepared inputs from those actually sent to the model.\nFile-discovery calls MUST count as tool calls without recording directory\nlistings as evidence or source inputs.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment:** the implementation satisfies `requirements.authoring.usage_inputs`, and the tests cover it. The one soft spot is that counts by evidence kind are derivable from per-input rows rather than stored as aggregates.\n\n**Implementation**\n- **Per-input record.** `UsageLog::prepared` (`src/authoring/usage.rs`, 142–176) appends one `InputUsage` row per input. Each row has an `origin`, a `kind`, UTF-8 `bytes`, `lines`, `components`, `unique`, `submitted_in_request` and `sent_in_request`.\n  - `origin` is `\"mandatory\"`, `\"habeas\"` or `\"ripgrep\"`.\n  - `kind` is `outline`, `requirements` or `definition`.\n  - `bytes` sums the `str::len` of each text line plus the newline separators. `lines` is the length of the text array.\n  - `components` is `matches.len()` for a requirements input, so the matched-declaration count is recorded. It defaults to 1 for other kinds.\n  - Counts and sizes by kind are therefore recorded per input, with mandatory and additional inputs distinguished by origin.\n- **Unique versus repeated.** `unique` comes from a `BTreeSet` insert of the input's serialized JSON. A re-read is marked `unique: false`, including a re-read of a mandatory input through `habeas`.\n- **Successful versus failed reads.** In `assess`, a successful dispatch calls `usage.tool(name, false)` and then `usage.prepared(...)`. A failed dispatch calls `usage.tool(name, true)` and records no input. Failures are counted per tool in `tool_failures`.\n- **Prepared versus sent.**\n  - `begin_request` stamps `submitted_in_request` on every prepared input.\n  - `end_request` stamps `sent_in_request` only when the provider returned usage, meaning the request completed.\n  - Failed or throttled attempts therefore leave inputs submitted but not sent, and a later successful retry marks them sent.\n  - `configured_record` prepares the mandatory inputs and saves before connecting to the provider.\n- **File discovery.** `tools::list_files`, `outline` and `references` return `inputs: Vec::new()`. `assess` still calls `usage.tool(...)` for them, so they count as tool calls and add no input rows.\n- **Marking.** The `{impl}` markers cover `InputUsage`, `prepared`, `begin_request`, `end_request`, `tool`, `skipped_tool`, `assess` and `configured_record`. I found no unmarked code implementing this requirement and no unspecified behavior in the marked code. The `components`, `submitted_in_request` and `sent_in_request` fields serve the matched-declaration count and the prepared-versus-sent distinction.\n\n**Tests**\n- `input_metadata_counts_components_and_reads_without_persisting_source` (`usage.rs`) covers:\n  - the `outline` kind;\n  - UTF-8 byte counting with a multibyte `λ`;\n  - line count;\n  - `components` equal to 2 for a requirements input with two matches;\n  - `unique` true then false for a repeated `habeas` read;\n  - origin;\n  - the null → submitted → sent transitions;\n  - that no source text or names are persisted.\n- `failed_submission_can_be_confirmed_on_a_\nlater_attempt` covers a failed request leaving `sent_in_request` null, then a retry setting it.\n- `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text` covers tool calls versus failures versus skips, and that no inputs are recorded for tool calls alone.\n- `throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt` (`mod.rs`) covers 8 failed attempts then a success, with `submitted_in_request` 0 and `sent_in_request` 8.\n- The CLI test `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` (`tests/authoring_cli.rs`) covers the end-to-end path:\n  - a `list_files` call counts toward `tool_call_count` of 6;\n  - a failed `habeas` read gives `tool_failures.habeas` of 1;\n  - a repeated `habeas` read is recorded as `unique == false` and sent in request 1;\n  - mandatory inputs of kind `definition` have bytes greater than 0;\n  - the usage JSON contains no source content.\n- `tools.rs` tests assert that `list_files`, `outline` and `references` return empty inputs.\n\n**Minor observations**\n- Counts by kind are not stored as aggregates and have to be derived from the per-input rows. I read the requirement as satisfied by the per-input rows.\n- No test pins `components` for a real mandatory requirements input. The unit test uses a synthetic input shaped like the real one (`matches`, `text`), and `inputs.rs` tests confirm that real mandatory inputs have that shape.\n- There are no acknowledged FIXMEs for this requirement.",
  "inputs": [
